WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.840
INTRO:
Recently, you may have heard that Russia may

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.169
be loosening restrictions on piracy in an
effort to combat all of the tech sanctions

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:09.430
that have been placed on their citizens.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:14.140
This makes sense as basically every tech and
media company you can think of has sanctioned

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.020
Russia so in order to continue being productive
and get some entertainment, Russia basically

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.650
has to turn to piracy.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.590
But, something that you may not have expected
though is that there are rumors and speculation

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:31.250
floating around that Biden may not only loosen
restrictions surrounding piracy, but he may

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.809
legalize piracy altogether in America with
an upcoming executive order.

00:00:35.809 --> 00:00:39.629
Ever since these rumors surfaced, pirates
from around the world have rejoiced as this

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:42.890
move could spark an international copyright
revolution.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.230
In the meantime, production studios have been
mortified as they struggle to understand how

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.190
the billions they spent on lobbying failed
to prevent this.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:55.249
So, here’s the reasoning behind why Biden
may be introducing this legislation, the details

00:00:55.249 --> 00:01:00.409
about what it may include, and its potential
short and long-term repercussions.

00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:06.300
DEFLATION CRISIS:
Starting with the reasoning for such a move,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.539
we have the deflation crisis.

00:01:08.539 --> 00:01:12.780
As you guys know, over the past year, deflation
has gone through the roof.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:17.759
Now, this may be confusing at first given
that CPI readings would suggest the exact

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:19.060
opposite.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:24.990
For example, the most recent CPI reading suggested
an inflation rate of 7.9% which is the highest

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.820
we’ve seen in 4 decades.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.479
Also, let’s not forget that gas prices are
literally $7 a gallon in some parts of the

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:32.479
country.

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:37.040
But, as Jerome has been preaching from the
start, this slight increase in prices is just

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.040
transitory.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.240
So, gas prices should stabilize at $6.50 any
day now.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.909
In the meantime, the commodities of our era
have been deflating faster than ever before.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:49.689
Take Apple for example.

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:53.630
People often complain about how expensive
Apple products have become as many of their

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.850
products cost well over a $1000.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.609
They even sell a monitor stand for $1000.

00:01:58.609 --> 00:02:04.039
But, the thing that people forget to consider
is that Apple has yet to raise prices on any

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:06.420
of these products despite rampant inflation.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:14.210
A $1000 in 2019 is equivalent to $1109 today,
yet Apple still only charges a $1000 for the

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:15.210
stand.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.470
This means that the Pro stand has dropped
in price by roughly 10%.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:25.030
Now, 10% may not sound like much, but when
you’re talking about $50,000 Mac Pro, you’re

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.430
actually getting a $5000 discount.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:33.710
So, as Cathie Wood was suggesting, the real
fear is not inflation but actually deflation.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.330
But what does deflation have to do with piracy?

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.970
Well, during a deflation crisis, cash is king
and unfortunately, most millennials have on

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:42.970
cash.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.060
This isn’t all that surprising given that
the average millennial would rather water

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.780
their plants than handle finances, but it
does pose a serious problem.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:55.460
As baby boomers retire and cut back on spending,
millennials are becoming the workhorse of

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.460
the economy.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.810
But given that most of them are broke, we’ll
see less capital flowing into dogecoin, Shiba

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.660
Inu, Floki Inu, and the leading NFTs.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.300
So, Biden’s potential executive order is
simply attempting to curb this decline.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:12.340
If millennials no longer have to pay for their
17 media and entertainment subscriptions every

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.170
month, they can actually save a substantial
amount of money.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:19.140
Now, it’s not like they’re gonna save
this for retirement, but proponents of this

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.760
executive order are hoping that they turn
around and spend this money on something more

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.760
lucrative.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.970
You see, media companies aren’t the most
lucrative businesses.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:32.060
Disney, for example, hasn’t been able to
crack a 5% net margin since the pandemic started.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.300
Meanwhile, Starbucks has been holding strong
at a 15% net margin which is 3 times higher.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.680
So, if millennials spend more money at Starbucks
instead of paying for media, which is probably

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.990
where they’ll spend it, corporate America
as a whole can generate more profits.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.260
Corporate America can then turn around and
invest this extra money into real assets such

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:51.650
as stocks, real estate, bonds, and commodities
like the Mac Pro which will hopefully curb

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.760
the impacts of the deflation crisis.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:59.000
EXECUTIVE ORDER #02496:
Now that we’ve discussed the reasoning behind

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.740
this potential executive order, let’s delve
into the meat of the legislation itself.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:08.800
The first rumors of such a move surfaced from
the official TFES Twitter account at 7:37

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:09.800
AM.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:15.150
They tweeted quote, “Watch out for Biden’s
potential Executive Order #02496.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.320
Piracy may be legalized very soon.”

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.290
At first, people didn’t really know what
this meant, but soon enough, more and more

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.820
tweets started to surface.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.430
Tony Stark, for example, tweeted “Haha.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.600
Good thing I called it with Endgame years
ago.”

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.320
Shortly after, Elon Musk tweeted, “Does
this mean no more Iron Man cameos?”

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.810
Meanwhile, Facebook tweeted, “Too bad the
movie industry didn’t embrace the data collection

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.810
model.”

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.340
All of these cryptic tweets were still quite
confusing to put together, but eventually,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.590
we saw a new Wikipedia page pop up that gave
details into the executive order.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:50.210
The Wikipedia page describes the deflation
threat that’s looming over the United States

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.570
and how Biden has little choice but to pass
this executive order.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:58.560
If this executive order were to pass, piracy
of all movies, games, software, and music

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.340
would become perfectly legal within the United
States.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:05.240
On top of this, all convicted pirates will
be cleared of all charges and released from

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.240
prison.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.720
Now, you may be wondering, if no one is paying
for media, then no production company will

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.530
want to produce any content right?

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:17.840
Well, that’s what everyone thought at first
including Tony Stark, but fortunately, a powerful

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.080
individual has stepped up to the plate.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.460
The executive order outlines that any and
all production activities will be personally

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.320
funded by Jerome’s money printer.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:31.120
Jerome figured that with deflation getting
out of hand, printing some extra cash can’t

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.120
hurt.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.010
Also, production costs amongst even the biggest
production studios are peanuts for Jerome.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:41.830
Disney, for example, was planning on spending
$33 billion on content in 2022.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:47.550
For Jerome, $33 billion is just a day of printing
if that, so it doesn’t look like production

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.860
studios will run into any funding issues anytime
soon.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.900
One thing to note though is that Jerome will
only cover production costs and that he won’t

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.260
be paying for profits.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:59.770
So, these production studios still have to
figure out how to monetize their viewers to

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:04.490
generate profits, but moving forward they’ll
never have to worry about recouping production

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:05.490
costs.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:10.470
It’s just a matter of how much profits can
they generate.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.100
REPERCUSSIONS:
With such a game-changing piece of legislation,

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.790
there’s no doubt that we’ll see massive
short-term and long-term repercussions.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:22.240
One of the first moves we’ve seen production
companies take is initiating massive bidding

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.070
wars for all of the most popular piracy sites.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:30.800
Now, if this legislation passes, Netflix,
Disney, Hulu, and all the other popular streaming

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.210
platforms will have download links to all
of their content on their websites themselves.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.470
But, it seems like a lot of people prefer
to use the classic piracy sites over these

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.700
offerings, hence the bidding war.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:47.139
KickAssTorrents for example was recently acquired
by an undisclosed party for $32 billion.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:51.410
Meanwhile, the Pirate Bay has apparently received
dozens of private offers with the highest

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.940
offer clocking in at over $100 billion.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:59.750
This is quite ironic given that just a few
hours ago, acquiring any one of these sites

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:04.250
would’ve been unthinkable given the insane
liabilities that each of them carries.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:08.230
Also, we should note that the executive order
hasn’t even been passed yet.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:12.210
So, these bidders are taking quite a risk
by prematurely acquiring these sites, but

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.590
I guess they can afford it.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:18.410
Given the size of the offers, I think it’s
likely that the offer is either from Netflix

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:23.669
or Disney, but then again, it could just as
easily be from Google or Facebook as well

00:07:23.669 --> 00:07:28.140
given that this is the perfect opportunity
to capitalize on the trend towards piracy.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:32.320
While Artem Vaulin, KickAssTorrents founder,
quickly agreed to sell KickAssTorrents, the

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.060
same cannot be said about the Pirate Bay’s
Founders.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:40.120
For them, running the Pirate Bay is less about
making money and more about principle.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.820
One of the Pirate Bay’s co-founders, Frederick
Neij has literally said that spending time

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.200
in prison was well worth for the Pirate Bay.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:50.370
So, it’s not surprising that they weren’t
enticed to sell out to big tech.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:54.820
Not to mention, they can likely make a lot
more money if they simply went public which

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:56.060
seems to be the plan.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:58.760
Gottfrid Svartholm tweeted, “Mark your calendars.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.880
The Pirate Bay may have an IPO on April 20.”

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.970
If this actually does end up taking place,
the Pirate Bay will evolve into being one

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.900
of the largest companies in the world basically
overnight.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:13.710
Also, given that the three co-founders currently
own all the equity in the company, they’ll

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.900
each likely become multi-deca billionaires.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.060
So, the future is looking pretty bright for
both production companies and piracy sites

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.710
alike, but only time will tell who will become
the biggest pirate.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:30.380
PUBLIC RESPONSE:
In terms of the response to this legislation,

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.289
companies seem to be all over the place.

00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:37.029
Adobe, for example, tweeted “Eh, it’s
not like it makes a difference to us anyway.”

00:08:37.029 --> 00:08:42.519
Meanwhile, Disney has promised a full-on press
meeting to hash out their plan moving forward.

00:08:42.519 --> 00:08:46.529
If they’re able to acquire a large piracy
site like The Pirate Bay, it’s likely that

00:08:46.529 --> 00:08:50.740
Disney will shift to displaying ads and collecting
data similar to Google and Facebook.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:55.249
They’ll probably also continue to offer
their movies in theaters for a fee if people

00:08:55.249 --> 00:08:56.249
are interested.

00:08:56.249 --> 00:09:00.660
As for the public, most pirates don’t really
care all that much.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:06.439
The biggest upside for them is that they no
longer have to pay for a VPN, but then again

00:09:06.439 --> 00:09:10.709
if Disney and Netflix start to collect data
through piracy sites, it’s probably best

00:09:10.709 --> 00:09:12.480
to use a VPN anyway.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.139
So, it doesn’t really make a difference
to most pirates.

00:09:15.139 --> 00:09:20.129
Meanwhile, we’ve seen a lot of piracy noobs
navigating to rip-off sites of the Pirate

00:09:20.129 --> 00:09:23.699
Bay, downloading various viruses, and falling
for the stupidest of scams.

00:09:23.699 --> 00:09:28.130
It’s probably best if these guys stick to
paying for their media until companies come

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.279
out with their own download portals.

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:34.160
In terms of countrywide responses, Russia
has perceived this as a challenge.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:39.589
After all, they were the first world power
to loosen restrictions on piracy.

00:09:39.589 --> 00:09:45.769
In an effort to stay one step ahead of the
US, it’s expected that Putin will announce

00:09:45.769 --> 00:09:50.269
that Russia will not only allow for the piracy
of media but also the piracy of intellectual

00:09:50.269 --> 00:09:51.269
property.

00:09:51.269 --> 00:09:56.180
In other words, all patents and trademarks
will become void meaning that anyone can copy,

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:57.949
produce and sell anything.

00:09:57.949 --> 00:10:03.019
Such a policy seems too woke to be adopted
by the US right now, but if the US enters

00:10:03.019 --> 00:10:07.259
a piracy war with Russia, we may see similar
policies surfacing very soon.

00:10:07.259 --> 00:10:09.429
But we’ll just have to wait and see.

00:10:09.429 --> 00:10:11.290
Do you guys support this executive order?

